        "created_at": "2026-09-09T12:42:52.934Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello WoW Development Team,</p>\n<p>I am a veteran EU player posting here on the US Bug Report forums following the explicit advice of a very kind Game Master (from a recent ticket regarding my main character, <strong>Xanatas, Nemesis-EU realm</strong>). The GM validated my situation but explained that Customer Support lacks the tools to manually alter legacy achievements from 2014, suggesting that I document my edge case here for the developers.</p>\n<p>I am purposefully posting on the US forums because I understand this platform receives much more direct attention from the core development team. To do this, I have specifically created a level 1 Warlock character here on the US realms named Xanatas and fortunately, the name was available!</p>\n<p>I am missing the <strong>“Breaker of the Black Harvest” Feat of Strength (ID: 9016)</strong> and the associated legacy title <strong>“of the Black Harvest”</strong>. I am only pressing on out of pure love for my Warlock, a character I have cherished for so many years. Honestly, trying to get my well-deserved title posthumously is starting to feel even harder than defeating Kanrethad back in 2014! As you can probably tell, this title truly means the world to me.</p>\n<p>I have been trying to resolve this matter for many years. In fact, back during Warlords of Draenor, I managed to speak directly via in-game chat with a Game Master about this issue. Even back then, that GM expressed deep regret and acknowledged how much I cared about the title, but explained they lacked the specific tools to manually bypass the automated script failure at that time. Unfortunately, although I am not an insistent person by nature, I feel forced to press on because I have read about several other Warlocks in my exact situation who successfully managed to have their title granted.</p>\n<p>This is a well-known historical script issue, but my account has a very specific timeline:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>The MoP Era:</strong> I successfully defeated Kanrethad and unlocked the Green Fire during Mists of Pandaria, well before the pre-patch deadline. At the time, my Warlock was a <strong>Human</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>The 6.0.2 Script Bug:</strong> My subscription expired right before Patch 6.0.2 was deployed. My account remained completely inactive (no game time) during the entire pre-patch window. Because of this, the automated retroactive script entirely skipped my character.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Subsequent Race Changes:</strong> Years later, I performed multiple Race Changes on this Warlock, eventually becoming a <strong>Void Elf</strong>. These updates have likely hidden the original MoP quest completion flags from standard GM tools.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>My EU Warlock <strong>actively possesses and uses the Green Fire ability (The Codex of Xerrath)</strong>. However, my profile has no modern quest completion logs for this chain. Since there is no record of me completing the quest in recent years, but the Green Fire is active, it shows that it was completed prior to the 6.0.2 deadline. Furthermore, my transaction history confirms my account was frozen during that exact pre-patch window.</p>\n<p>I respectfully request a developer to review this legacy account flag discrepancy and manually restore the Feat of Strength and title that my character rightfully earned over a decade ago.</p>\n<p>Thank you very much for your time and for looking into a veteran player’s case</p>",
